+"""Verified generator for a rank-one mixed Groebner-basis problem.
+
+The paper's q-Fractional Groebner Basis Problem becomes the traditional problem
+when q=1 (Section 2).  This module stays in that native polynomial setting.  It
+samples the reduced basis first and then applies a full-rank linear change of
+generators, so generation never solves the emitted instance.
+
+The family is deliberately Track B.  Generic exact row reduction recovers the
+basis in polynomial time.  The no-tool challenge is to notice the shared
+quadratic sum and undo its rank-one mixing with only one normalized equation per
+variable.
+"""
+
