   540	\noindent \textbf{Stage 2. Polynomial Encoding. } Define a polynomial system based on $(\mathcal{P}, \mathcal{L})$ as follows. Create a variable $y_i$ corresponding to the $i$th literal of $\mathcal{L}$. Denote this set of variables by $Y$. Create a polynomial $y_i(1-y_i)$. This gives a set of $|\mathcal{L}|$ ``literal polynomials" whose mutual roots are exactly $\{0,1\}^{|\mathcal{L}|}$. 
